WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:06.220
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and today
I'm revealing 36 devilish details you missed

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:10.440
in Lucifer Season 5
from crazy easter eggs to hilarious meta references

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:15.079
and and ingenious production design.
Spoiler altert, it is gonna be epic.

00:00:15.079 --> 00:00:20.130
The third episode of Season 5 is perhaps one
of the funniest in the series so far as Lucifer

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.929
and Chloe investigate a murder on the set
of ¡Diablo!,

00:00:22.929 --> 00:00:27.660
a network TV procedural show that's an hilariously
OTT version of Lucifer.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.710
Some of the jokes are more obvious riffs on
the characters we know and love

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:35.270
"Like I keep telling you, Detective Doofus..."
a reference to Lucifer's "Detective Douche"

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:38.230
nickname for Dan.
But others are a bit more subtle, such as

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:42.539
the show's billboard with Diablo's name in
neon lights, just like the original Season

00:00:42.539 --> 00:00:44.100
1 Lucifer poster.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.770
And then there's Diablo's version of Lucifer's
mojo power:

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.239
"You want to find the killer, figure out their
yearning."

00:00:49.239 --> 00:00:50.910
Right.
Isn't there a better word for that?"

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:55.859
Although Luci evidently doesn't like the word
"yearn", he did actually say it himself in

00:00:55.859 --> 00:00:59.450
Season 1 when he used his mojo against a corrupt
LAPD detective.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:03.780
"What do you yearn for in that...
rotten soul of yours?"

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.610
When Ella finds the murder weapon that killed
Diablo, she calls it "the only blade that

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:11.030
can kill the Devil".
This is actually a sneaky reference to Azrael's

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:15.670
Blade which featured heavily in the Season
2 episode "Trip To Stabby Town" where it got

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:19.320
close to killing Lucifer when Dan wielded
it in anger against him.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.242
In episode 2, Chloe can see Michael isn't
really acting like Lucifer normally would,

00:01:23.242 --> 00:01:28.640
and she tries to get him to do something typically
inappropriate by giving him Dan's dessert

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.200
to eat.
"Is that my pudding?

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.860
Yes, here you go Daniel.
OK.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:35.030
What's your game?
Did you spit in it?

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:37.829
He spit in it."
The issue of Lucifer pinching his pudding

00:01:37.829 --> 00:01:42.220
has been a recurring joke throughout the series
ever since Luci stole it in Season 2.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:47.430
"I know you ate my pudding!"
And another time, Dan even discovered that

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:50.110
Luci's mum, Charlotte, was also stealing his
pudding.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:54.850
In fact, there was a whole episode in Season
3 devoted to a crime that occurred at the

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:57.250
dessert factory:
"Pudding Plus is my favorite, okay?

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:01.860
Twice as much protein as all the other brands."
But poor Dan, never really gets a break, because

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:06.490
when the real Lucifer returns from Hell in
Season 5, he starts using Dan's mug for his

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:09.130
whiskey drinking at the police precinct.

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:13.351
The noir episode is a lot of fun with loads
of easter eggs and references hidden in the

00:02:13.351 --> 00:02:16.690
background.
When Lucifer and P.I. Jack Monroe go to visit

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:21.570
Willy the Sausage Prince, they find him getting
his portrait painted while ridiculously dressed

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.300
as a knight.
And if you take a closer look on the walls,

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:28.360
there are lots more portraits of Willy,
who clearly sees and models himself after

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:33.210
old European royalty because there's a portrait
of him in the exact same style as a famous

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:37.580
painting of England's King Henry VIII,
and there's another portrait of him that looks

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:42.860
very much like the style of this painting
of the French King Francis I.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:47.650
Then there's the nightclub where Lily Rose,
aka Lilith, sings which is appropriately named

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:50.450
the "Garden Club"
because Lilith originally lived with Adam

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:54.230
in the Garden of Eden and kept a piece of
the garden in her ring.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:59.980
And her flowery name in the show, Lily Rose,
is another nice nod to her Garden of Eden

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:00.980
origins.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:05.550
Inside the club behind the bar is Al Capone's
machine gun with a plaque that reads: "Thanks

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.370
For Listening".
Of course, customers sometimes pour their

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:11.950
problems out to bartenders who have a reputation
as sympathetic listeners,

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:16.560
so it's no coincidence that Linda, who's a
therapist in the modern-day world of Lucifer,

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.840
turns out to be the bartender at the club
Al Capone frequented.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:25.480
But there's an extra layer to this reference
because the noir episode is set in 1946,

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:29.330
which is the same year that the real-life
Capone was examined by a psychiatrist who

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:32.880
declared that the mobster "had the mentality
of a 12-year-old child".

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:37.510
Oh, and, when the bartender pours Lucifer
a drink, we get another little shout-out to

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:41.790
actress Rachel Harris's usual role in the
show and how Lucifer normally addresses her

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:46.670
as "Doctor" when Luci says:
"Oh, lovely. Just what the doctor ordered."

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:50.820
In episode 2, just before Chloe reveals to
Michael that she knows who he really is, she

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:54.160
shows him the bullet necklace Lucifer gave
to her in Season 3.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:58.400
"It's the bullet from when you shot me.
Remember in the warehouse, early in our partnership?"

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.820
Chloe showing the bullet to Michael just before
she shoots him in the leg, exactly like she

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:07.690
did to Lucifer in Season 1, is a delicious
detail that proves Michael can't fool her.

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:12.500
"Once I shot Lucifer to prove he was the Devil,
and now I'm shooting you to prove you're not."

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:16.380
Interestingly, Michael betrayed himself in
his reaction when Chloe showed him the necklace,

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:20.810
because if you re-watch the moment, there's
a slight flicker of hesitation when she mentions

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:22.960
it:
"See?

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:26.460
Still have it on.
I can see that."

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:30.560
And on top of that, because Michael doesn't
know what the bullet necklace is, he also

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:35.310
doesn't realise that Chloe is technically
lying when she says she still has it on,

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:39.470
because she actually took the necklace off
towards the end of Season 3 when she got together

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:42.940
with Pierce and didn't wear it at all in Season
4.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:47.500
After Lucifer and Chloe sleep together for
the first time, he asks her whether she feels

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:51.870
cold, making a joke about how in the first
season Chloe was adamant she'd never have

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:56.290
sex with him.
"I will never, ever, ever sleep with you.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:59.070
Never."
"Playing hard to get, I like it."

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:02.850
"When Hell freezes over, Lucifer."
And notice that when Chloe arrives at Luci's

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:06.970
place that night, she's dressed in red, a
colour of passion and love, of course, but

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:09.650
also a colour closely associated with the
devil!

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:14.140
In the show, Lucifer often wears a little
red pocket square and the soles of his shoes

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:17.340
are also coloured red.
In fact, we saw only last season how the show's

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:21.140
costume department played on that colour association
in Eve's clothes

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:26.750
which went from being heavenly white to various
shades of red after she reconnected with Lucifer.

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:31.280
The morning after when Chloe wakes up, she
asks Luci if she was "snoring like a truck

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:36.900
driver".
She doesn't let him reply, but the moment

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:41.170
is a nice call-back to Season 1 when she woke
up in Lucifer's bed after getting drunk the

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:44.650
night before.
That time, nothing actually happened between

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:48.290
them, but as she leaves Lucifer tells her:
"You snore, by the way.

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:50.820
Like an Albanian field wench!"

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:56.250
Another funny Season 5 moment comes when Maze
decides to style herself exactly like Ella

00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:00.020
in an effort to try and be nicer and learn
how to become more emotionally available,

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:03.660
as Dr Linda suggested.
"Oh, my God, I have that exact same shirt!"

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:04.660
"Yes, you did!"
"Wait.

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:08.630
Did you steal my clothes?"
Maze doesn't just get Ella's look down to

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:12.170
a T, she also hilariously tries to imitate
Ella's mannerisms.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:17.630
And that moment reminds me of other such humorous
times on the show, including Season 2 when

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:21.890
Lucifer decided to "learn how to douche" and
dressed up and tried to be like Dan.

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:24.100
"Where to now, Twinsy?
Hmm?"

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:28.100
And then there was the time in Season 4 that
Eve dressed up as Chloe and also copied her

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:31.480
body language to try and get Lucifer's attention.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:36.450
In Season 5, Ella almost seems to find her
geeky soulmate in Pete when he turns up with

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:40.700
tickets for a Star Trek convention and they
both start having a conversation in Klingon,

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:44.900
a funny little call-back to when Ella tried
to talk to Chloe in the fictional language

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:47.000
in Season 2:
"Ta' vonlu!"

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:50.740
"Ta' von what?"
"It's Klingon for 'the king is trapped.'

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:54.900
In Star Trek they play three-dimensional chess."
And there's an even geekier detail in the

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:59.370
clothes Ella wears to the convention.
Her uniform is blue, which is the colour worn

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:03.950
by science and medical personnel in Star Trek,
and that fits our Ella perfectly as she's

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:16.660
a forensic scientist.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:56.790
There must be some big Stanley Kubrick fans
among the Lucifer crew as Season 5 has visual

00:07:56.790 --> 00:08:00.300
shout-outs to not one but two of the iconic
filmmaker's movies.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:06.030
In episode 2, Chloe's investigation into murderous
goings-on in a tech billionaire's space simulation

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:10.660
provides the perfect opportunity for a tribute
to 2001: A Space Odyssey.

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:14.580
The story kicks off with a call-back to the
film's spaceship and its sleek monochrome

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:19.590
design and the image of an astronaut making
their way up an octagonal walkway.

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:24.200
The next Kubrick reference pops up in episode
7 when Chloe and Lucifer head to the home

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:28.820
of a man they believe to be a serial killer.
Some Shining-esque music plays in the background

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.600
as a little boy pedals down a corridor on
a tricycle.

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:35.300
"Well, that bodes well."
Just as Danny Torrance rode around the corridors

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:39.880
of the Overlook Hotel in The Shining.
And the wallpaper in the apartment block corridor

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:45.080
also has vibes of The Shining hotel's carpet
about it, with its geometric pattern and orange

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.960
and brown colouring.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:47.960
When Michael strides into the middle of a
shoot-out between Chloe and a bunch of bad

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:48.960
guys, he whistles the theme to the show.
Which Chloe immediately recognises because

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:49.960
this isn't the first time that tune has featured
in an episode.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:50.960
Yes, back during a case involving a murdered
musician in season 2, Lucifer wrote a song

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:51.960
for Chloe that perfectly sums up both his
role in their partnership and the show's premise:

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:52.960
♪ Crime-solving Devil ♪
♪ It makes sense ♪

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:53.960
♪ Don't over think it ♪
Intriguingly, the plot of that season 2 episode

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:54.960
also involved Lucifer returning to LA out
of the blue after having spent time in hell

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:55.960
to save Chloe,
a situation which nicely mirrors the circumstances

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:56.960
in season 5, though this time it's Michael,
pretending to be Lucifer, who returns.

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:57.960
When Lilith is explaining to Lucifer the history
of her ring, she talks about how the Aztecs

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:58.960
threw her into a volcano.
"I survive, and...

00:08:58.960 --> 00:08:59.960
somebody writes it on a stone tablet.
You know how these things start."

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:00.960
"I do."
Her comment about stone tablets is a reference

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:05.120
to the Ten Commandments that God gave to Moses,
which were inscribed on two tablets of stone,

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:09.190
and which form the basis of many of the rules
in Judaism and Christianity.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:13.850
In the finale, Michael delights in preying
on Amenadiel's fears for his son Charlie,

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:18.020
really tapping into his anxiety about his
baby's ill health, growing up, and even his

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:21.360
mortality.
As Michael badgers Amenadiel about all this

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:26.130
and Lucifer joins in arguing against Michael,
we see the twins position themselves on either

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:29.730
side of their brother,
creating an image of a literal devil and angel

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:32.790
on Amenadiel's shoulders.
"But they grow up so fast."

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:34.600
"Don't listen to him, brother.
Don't let him get inside your head."

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:38.440
The interesting thing here is that the devil,
Lucifer, is the one appealing to Amenadiel's

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:43.480
better nature, while the angel, Michael, is
the one trying to make him indulge his worst

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:46.150
instincts.
Often in this angel-and-devil-on-the-shoulder

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:50.850
trope, the devil appears on the protagonist's
left side, as that's associated with evil,

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:56.320
while the angel appears on their right side;
however, here, Lucifer the devil is on Amenadiel's

00:09:56.320 --> 00:10:00.851
right, while Michael the angel is on Amenadiel's
left, reinforcing the fact that Lucifer and

00:10:00.851 --> 00:10:06.180
Michael act contrary to their prescribed roles.
This scene also reminds me of a similar moment

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:08.740
in Season 4.
"Lucifer, stop."

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:10.760
"Lucifer, do it."

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:15.570
When the killer's revealed in episode 6 during
a DJ set at Lux, it turns out to be a jealous

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:19.140
ex-husband.
And as he explains why he did it, green lights

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:23.190
swirl around him and there's even a shot that
makes it look as if they're radiating from

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:25.750
his head.
Of all the colours they could have chosen

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:30.010
to light this scene and frame the killer's
head, green is the perfect one as it's long

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:32.820
been associated with jealousy and envy.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:36.710
The crucial moment at the very end of the
penultimate episode sees Dan arrive with a

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:39.720
gun and proceed to shoot Lucifer right in
front of Chloe.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:44.321
Those with a keen ear might have noticed something
familiar about the soundtrack playing in the

00:10:44.321 --> 00:10:47.580
lead up to that moment.
Yes, if you're a fan of the critically acclaimed

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:52.540
Netflix series Dark you might have recognised
the song playing in the background as Inside,

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.500
which played in the third and final season
of Dark.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:59.810
The lyrics of the song, which plays subtly
in the background, perfectly rack up the tension

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:03.860
and enhance the dramatic build-up to Dan pulling
the trigger on Lucifer.

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:07.330
As a show Lucifer has always enjoyed making
meta references

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:11.590
"Sounds like a a soon-to-be-canceled TV show."
but in Season 5 there are so many that I'll

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:15.240
list some of the best here.
After Ella discovers that Chloe and Lucifer

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:19.750
have finally had sex, she explains her reaction
in the same way that many of the fandom's

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:22.580
Deckerstar shippers may well have felt before
that moment.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:25.580
"I was so ready to have my Deckerstar dreams
crushed again."

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.470
"Why?"
"'Cause it's been one bummer after another

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:29.080
with you two.
I didn't want to get my hopes up."

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:33.770
And the tagline of the ¡Diablo! TV show is
'Don't tell HIM the Devil made you do it!'

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:37.990
which is a reference back to Lucifer's complaints
earlier in the series about humans trying

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:40.800
to pin the blame for their sins on him all
the time:

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:45.010
"'Oh, the Devil made me do it.'
I have never made any one of them do anything."

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:49.280
Which is why it's particularly funny when
Ella quotes the tagline back at Lucifer:

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:54.970
"Don't tell him the Devil made you do it."
And there's the moment when Lucifer comments

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:58.800
about the actor who plays Diablo and the script
notes he made about his character.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:03.640
"He had a fascinating insight into the character.
Some wild theories about self-loathing, but

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:06.790
we can't get it all right."
This is, of course, a joke about Lucifer and

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:11.310
how his own self-hatred and sense of guilt
came to a head in Season 4, causing him to

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:15.990
transform into his full devil form.
Although Luci eventually recognised his self-hatred

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:18.940
back then.
"Why do I hate myself so much?"

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:22.300
Now that reference seems to have flown completely
over his head.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:26.940
In the noir episode, down the alleyway outside
the Garden Club, there's a sign for the "Alibi

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:30.680
Room", a little in-joke for fans of procedural
shows like Lucifer.

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:37.240
A few other meta details are that KarnalGirl506,
one of Jed's jilted lovers, appears in Episode

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:42.110
506 of the series.
And in Episode 507, the fake Whisper Killer

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:47.520
lives in Unit 507.
Also Linda's daughter, Adriana Nassar, is

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:49.980
named after a Netflix Originals manager.

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:55.650
As you can see, Season 5 of Lucifer is really
packing in the call-backs to previous seasons,

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:58.970
so it's well worth making time for an epic
binge rewatch.

